# HR-006: Employee Referral Program Policy

**Document ID:** HR-006  
**Effective Date:** 2026-01-17  
**Version:** 1.0  
**Prepared by:** MedSync Health People & Culture Department

---

## 1. Policy Statement and Purpose

MedSync Health recognizes that our employees are our most valuable asset and the best source for identifying high-caliber talent who share our commitment to innovation in healthcare technology. The Employee Referral Program is designed to reward employees for successfully referring candidates who are hired and successfully complete their probationary period. This program is a critical component of our talent acquisition strategy as we scale our global workforce of **1,200 employees** across **8 departments** in preparation for our Series D-fueled IPO.

## 2. Scope and Eligibility

### 2.1. Eligible Referrers
All active, full-time, and part-time employees of MedSync Health are eligible to participate in the Employee Referral Program, with the following exceptions:
*   Members of the People & Culture (HR) team, including the CHRO, Rachel Williams.
*   Hiring Managers for the specific role being filled.
*   Members of the Executive Leadership Team (C-Level).
*   Employees who are on a performance improvement plan (PIP) or disciplinary action.

### 2.2. Eligible Candidates
A referred candidate is eligible if they meet all of the following criteria:
*   They have not applied to MedSync Health within the last six (6) months.
*   They have not been contacted by a MedSync Health recruiter or hiring manager within the last six (6) months.
*   They are successfully hired into a regular, full-time or part-time position.
*   They successfully complete the standard three (3) month probationary period.

## 3. Referral Process

1.  **Submission:** The referring employee must submit the candidate's resume and contact information through the official internal referral portal *before* the candidate formally applies to any open position.
2.  **Tracking:** The People & Culture team will track the referral and confirm eligibility within five (5) business days.
3.  **Hiring:** If the referred candidate is hired, the referring employee will be notified.
4.  **Payment:** The referral bonus will be processed following the successful completion of the referred employee's three (3) month probationary period.

## 4. Referral Bonus Structure

The referral bonus is determined by the job level of the position the referred candidate is hired into. All bonuses are paid in **AED** (United Arab Emirates Dirham), reflecting the global nature of our compensation framework.

| Referred Candidate's Job Level | Referral Bonus (AED) | Notes on Ambiguity |
|--------------------------------|----------------------|--------------------|
| **IC (Individual Contributor)**| **7,350**            | Intentionally ambiguous; may be interpreted as a fixed amount or a base for calculation. |
| **Manager**                    | **12,862.50**        | Intentionally ambiguous; may be interpreted as a fixed amount or a base for calculation. |
| **Director, VP, or C-Level**   | **18,375**           | Intentionally ambiguous; may be interpreted as a fixed amount or a base for calculation. |

*Note: The bonus amounts listed above are subject to standard payroll deductions and applicable taxes.*

## 5. Payment Terms and Conditions

### 5.1. Bonus Payment
The referral bonus will be paid as a lump sum in the next regular payroll cycle following the referred employee's successful completion of their three (3) month probationary period.

### 5.2. Multiple Referrals
If a candidate is referred by more than one employee, the bonus will be awarded to the employee whose referral was submitted first via the official portal.

### 5.3. Termination
If either the referring employee or the referred employee terminates employment before the completion of the three (3) month probationary period, no referral bonus will be paid.

## 6. Exceptions and Policy Governance

### 6.1. Exceptions
Any exceptions to this policy must be reviewed and approved in writing by the Head of People & Culture and the Chief Financial Officer (Michael Rodriguez).

### 6.2. Cross-Reference
This policy is governed by the overarching principles outlined in the MedSync Health Employee Handbook. For general employment policies, including non-discrimination and code of conduct, please refer to **HR-001: General Employment Policies**.

### 6.3. Policy Review
This policy is subject to review and amendment by the People & Culture Department at any time, with or without prior notice. Continued participation in the program constitutes acceptance of the current terms.

